Support to implementation of the newly adopted national policies on improving the inclusiveness and quality of education at system and school levels;
Support to expansion and integration of skills development and adolescent empowerment programs in formal education;
Collaboration with key national counterparts on improving data collection, knowledge generation, overall governance and financing for the purpose of advancing of the education reform (education sector review; MEIS)

Adolescents empowered through UPSHIFT workshops, Hackathon for Social Change and other innovative skill building programmes;
The implementation of adolescent-led or adolescent-focused initiatives supported;
Adolescents empowered through the programmes for development of social and emotional and other key skills in out-of-school environments.  "

- Implementation of successful border management actions funded by the WBIBM Facility, adapted to national needs, and in line with international and European migrant protection standards;
- Strengthening digitalization of ID management in the Western Balkans, in line with EU standards, leading to improved border management in the region;
-Enhancing of operational and analytical capacities of border management agencies to address and mitigate border security and transnational organized crime challenges in the mixed migration context;
-Border management procedures in the WB are gender, protection-sensitive and fundamental rights compliant, in line with EU and international standards

Improved capacity of the Institute for Social and Child Protection to oversee implementation of SCP standards;
Strengthened capacity of CSWs` professionals including for work with Roma community in a culturally-sensitive way;
Increased demand and access to social protection services and benefits by eligible Roma families in Montenegro.
System strengthening for improved support to migrant, asylum seeking and refugee children and families

The national campaign on protection of children from adversity focusing on protection from family violence and the prohibition of corporal punishment implemented;
National institutions and civil society organizations supported to combat child marriages and gender based violence through strengthening the institutional response and community mobilization;
National institutions and capacity of civil society organizations enhanced so to support parents in positive child discipline and counsel children;

Availability of EU compliant and regionally harmonized standard operating procedures (SoPs) for assisted voluntary return and reintegration (AVRR) in beneficiary countries;
Organisation of AVRR/cultural mediation trainings/workshops as per national needs;
AVRR outreach activities;
Undertaking AVRR activities (organisation of assisted voluntary return of migrants to their countries of origin and reintegration in their countries of origin).

*WB countries adopted legal, operational, and administrative frameworks and standards for the establishment of Advanced Passenger Information (API) system and cost effective API infrastructure with data sharing capacities in place;                                                                                                                                                                   
* Return mechanisms (voluntary and non-voluntary) as well as operational cooperation are established at the regional level, and along with the selected countries of origin; 
*Capacity building on provision of reintegration to readmitted nationals;
*Capacity building on understanding of EU experience and best practices on readmission;
* More resilient local communities are created and social cohesion is improved between dwellers and asylum seekers, refugees, migrants, people in need of international protection and  persons with other protection needs (such as unaccompanied minors, potential victims of trafficking in human beings and others);                                                                                                       * Identification, registration and referral of mixed migration flows at first and second points of contact and within the territory, as well as pre-screening and screening on nationalities is improved;
*Technical Support to the Ministry of Interior of Montenegro to upgrade the central registry of citizens

IDF project:
-produce gender sensitive gap analysis of existing reintegration mechanism;
-produce a manual on provision of reintegration assistance;
-organize trainings/workshops on integrated reintegration assistance;
-organize trainings for readmitted nationals on business plan creation;
-to  facilitate cooperation at local level (coordination mtgs)
WBCAP (Readmission facility project):
-Successful implementation by WB authorities of the readmission actions funded by the WBCAP Facility, as adapted to their needs and in line with international and European migrant protection standards
-Improved functional communication, negotiations and cooperation channels on readmission between WB Countries and priority CoOs 
-Improved protection-sensitive practices on return and readmission of WB and third country nationals in the WB 
-Strengthened and digitalized readmission cooperation between the EU and the WB, in line with international and EU standards

1.Provide expert assistance to the Ministry of Economic Development and Tourism in the preparation of various legal, strategic and policy documents in the area of entrepreneurship, competitiveness, investments, etc.; 
2. Provide further consultancy support to the selected Montenegrin municipalities in the preparation of strategic development plans; 
3. Provide assistance to the Ministry in the promotion and realization of various programme lines of technical and financial support to entrepreneurs and MSMEs; 
4. Provide support to the Ministry in the implementation of the concept of national brand and raising capacities of the staff in this field; 
5. Provide support to the Ministry in the development of the new legal and strategic framework for the development of clusters and craftsmanship;
6. Raise professional capacities of the Ministry's staff in the relevant sector fields.

Conduct a research on alternative and counternarratives for the prevention of violent extremism and ongoing expert advice is available to project implementers;
Train civil society, local journalists and/or media professionals across the WB in the Redirect Method;
Curate identified alternative and counternarrative videos;
Reach targeted audiences in pilot countries, Albania, BiH, Montenegro, Kosovo* and Serbia with positive alternative and counternarrative content;
Improve skills of key reconciliation actors in the WB to effectively reach a targeted audience with professional alternative and counternarrative campaigns addressing violent extremist and divisive narratives;
Facilitate further engagement of interfaith and multi-confessional platforms in using modern technology and the web to dispel myths and misconceptions about religious radicalization.

Temporary transit reception centre is established and operational 
